    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0632" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg460"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4044</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-24T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 24, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6077. Your 4726, April 19, 6 p.m. British Government is now instructing Spring Rice to propose that American, French,
                    and British representatives at Monrovia jointly advise Liberian Government to
                    break with Germany; promises such assistance as may be necessary.</p>
                <p>The suggestion of sending a ship or ships to Liberian waters seems good to the
                    Foreign Office who are consulting Admiralty and will give me answer later.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
